+
+# Desktop packaged product bundles use the sealed runtime
+
+English | [中文](guide.zh.md)
+
+## Change
+
+Desktop now treats a packaged product bundle as owned by the sealed runtime. Startup restores its selected profile layer after native recovery and removes a direct profile dependency whose package copy disappeared. Earlier releases could leave `@kingsoftcloud/agentkit-studio@<version>` in `package.json` after a failed install; the next `pnpm add` then queried npm for an unpublished version and failed before installing the requested plugin.
+
+## Migration
+
+1. Install the new Desktop build and start it once. It validates the packaged product copy, keeps the product bundle selected, and removes the stale direct dependency from `$DSH_HOME/profiles/desktop-agentkit-studio/package.json`.
+2. Confirm that the profile still lists `@kingsoftcloud/agentkit-studio` under `dsh.profile.bundles` and that it is absent from the profile `dependencies` object. The Host then resolves the product from the sealed runtime.
+3. Retry the plugin operation, for example `pnpm add dsh-purge` from the Plugins page. The operation should resolve only the requested plugin and record its own dependency.
